\section{Initialization and Magnetic Calibration}
\label{sec:startup-policy}
\subsection{One-time handoff}
\label{sec:proxy-handoff}
The measurement-only Mahony proxy runs during Cold and TunerWarm startup while
period and acceleration statistics settle. Normal handoff requires initialized
proxy tilt, the minimum startup interval, a trusted gravity branch, usable sea
statistics, and a magnetic reference when magnetic aiding is enabled.
A timeout relaxes readiness but still requires the upright gravity branch;
it is not an unconditional transition to Live.

The gravity check uses a world-frame acceleration EMA with
$\alpha_{g,k}=1-e^{-\Delta t_k/\SI{12}{s}}$; the first valid sample initializes the EMA state directly. Its gate is ignored until this world-frame average has run for
\SI{5}{s}. At handoff the MEKF receives proxy tilt and the
available yaw reference, initializes its translational states, and activates
the current OU schedule. Accelerometer-bias learning remains held during
magnetic acquisition/refinement. A sustained tilt exceeding $70^\circ$ for
\SI{0.35}{s} invokes a guarded reinitialization, with a \SI{3}{s} cooldown.

\subsection{Magnetic acquisition and refinement}
Magnetic acquisition uses proxy tilt rather than the MEKF. A yaw-stripped proxy frame supplies the initial reference; later
independent acquisition refines that reference. Following
initial acquisition, a \SI{30}{s} refinement window begins no earlier than
\SI{90}{s}; completing it releases the additional bias hold. These discrete
reference-setting operations are distinct from the continuous offset
correction below, which slews the measurement correction without resetting
attitude.

\label{sec:mag-two-stage}
